<HowtoLayout slug="kling-3-product-video-guide" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">A bottle can look convincing while its cap changes shape halfway through the shot. Write the product before the camera move, then inspect the whole clip. A prompt describes an object; it does not prove that the clip matches the product you sell.</p>

  <h2>How do you write Kling 3.0 prompts for product video?</h2>

  <p>Write Kling 3.0 prompts as a shot: describe the product’s material, shape, and label, place it on a surface, then specify the lighting and a camera move. In hubStudio, Kling takes a prompt only. For a clip that opens on your actual product photo, choose an engine with a start-frame input.</p>

